{
  "_notes": [
    "Gottlieb System 1 shared map for early single-player solid-state titles using the reverse decimal-digit high-score layout.",
    "Covers Joker Poker, Torch, Genie, Sinbad, Totem, Hulk, Close Encounters, Charlie's Angels, Buck Rogers, Pinball Pool, Roller Disco, Solar Ride, and Asteroid Annie.",
    "These ROMs were formerly misclassified under maps/williams/system3/torch.map.json with platform williams-system4.",
    "Score/high-score digits are stored one decimal digit per byte in reverse order.",
    "Persisted high score (0x1A0-0x1A5) and credits (0x102) live in NVRAM and are verified against dumps. Live game_state (player scores 0x80-0x97, game_over 0x00) lives in volatile RAM, so it is not present in .nv dumps and must be confirmed against a live capture."
  ],
